<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via overnight system RPs Wed.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via overnight system RPs Wed.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve, as expected, added reserves to the banking system via a round of overnight system repurchase agreements (RPs) on Wednesday, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York confirmed.</p>
<p>Fed funds were trading at 5.69 percent, above the Fed's current official target level of 5.50 percent.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660))</p>
